use ../../../lib/UiComponent

export ui-component Marquee:
    description:
        A marquee moves a strip of content steadily across the screen by
        itself, such as partner logos or a short announcement, looping round
        so it never seems to end. The user doesn't move it along.

    movement:
        The content moves at a steady speed in one direction, across or up and
        down. Across follows the language's direction, so it is reversed for
        right-to-left languages, and the component can reverse it. The speed
        is set by the component, and more content doesn't make it move faster.

    copies:
        Copies of the content are added as needed, so there is never a gap
        and the loop is seamless. The copies are only for show. Assistive
        tools read the content once, and the keyboard only reaches the
        original.

    pausing:
        It pauses while the pointer is over it or focus is inside it, so the
        user can read or use what's there, and carries on when they leave. The
        component can also pause and restart it, and can start it paused.

    stopping:
        Because it keeps moving alongside other content, the user always has a
        way to stop it for good, such as a pause button, not just by hovering.

    reducedMotion:
        When the user has asked their device for less motion, it doesn't move,
        and the content is shown still.

    loops:
        It loops for ever, unless the component sets a number of times, after
        which it stops. It can wait a moment before it starts. The component
        is told each time a loop finishes, and when it stops.

    name:
        It has a name that assistive tools read out, saying what it holds,
        such as "Our partners". Its movement is never announced.

    edges:
        Whether the content fades out at the edges is up to the chosen
        library.

    nonGoals:
        - Not for anything the user must read or act on in time. Important
            information belongs somewhere that stays still
        - The user can't move it along or jump to an item. That's a Carousel
